---
layout: modern
permalink: /
---
<section class="intro" id="about">
  <img class="intro__photo" src="/assets/me.jpg" alt="Photo of Théodor Lemerle" width="600" height="799">
  <div class="intro__body">
    <h1>{{ site.name }}</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I did my PhD at <a href="https://www.ircam.fr/">IRCAM</a> (STMS lab, CNRS / Sorbonne Université)
        in the Analysis/Synthesis team, supervised by
        <a href="https://www.ircam.fr/person/axel-roebel">Axel Roebel</a> and
        <a href="https://www.ircam.fr/person/nicolas-obin">Nicolas Obin</a>.
        My thesis, <em>Toward Expressive and Long-Form Speech Synthesis</em>
        (<a href="{{ site.defense }}">defense video</a>), set out to build
        text-to-speech (TTS) models that can convincingly tell a story to a child.
        We proposed methods for control of high-level attributes (eg. emotions, prosody) under scarce
        annotated data regime. We also introduced architectures for stable synthesis with no measurable
        degradation over hours of speech, while being fully streamable in text and audio.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before that, I studied acoustics, signal processing and computer science for music
        (<a href="https://www.atiam.ircam.fr/en/">ATIAM</a>) at IRCAM, and mathematics and
        computer science for machine learning at Sorbonne Université (<a href="https://m2a.lip6.fr/">M2A</a>).
      </p>
      <p>
        My interests encompass: generative modeling, representation learning, efficient generation
        (eg. fast, low-latency, streamable) with a particular focus on speech and TTS.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="publications">
  <h2 class="section-title">Publications</h2>
  {% for group in publications | byYear %}
  <div class="pubyear">
    <h3 class="pubyear__label">{{ group.year }}</h3>
    <ol class="pubs">
      {% for p in group.items %}
      <li class="pub">
        <p class="pub__title">{{ p.title }}</p>
        <p class="pub__authors">{{ p.authors | replace("Théodor Lemerle", "<strong>Théodor Lemerle</strong>") | safe }}</p>
        <p class="pub__venue">{{ p.venueFull }}</p>
        <p class="pub__meta">
          <span class="venue"><span class="venue__name">{{ p.venueShort }}</span><span class="venue__kind venue__kind--{{ p.presentation | lower }}">{{ p.presentation }}</span></span>
          {% for l in p.links %}<a class="pill" href="{{ l.url }}">{{ icons[l.icon or "link"] | safe }}{{ l.label }}</a>{% endfor %}
        </p>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</section>

<section id="demos">
  <h2 class="section-title">Audio demos</h2>
  <div class="cards">
    {% for d in site.demos %}
    <a class="card" href="{{ d.url }}">
      <span class="card__title">{{ d.title }}{% if d.external %} ↗{% endif %}</span>
      <span class="card__desc">{{ d.description }}</span>
    </a>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

<section id="contact">
  <h2 class="section-title">Contact</h2>
  <p class="contact">
    <a class="contact__mail" data-email data-u="{{ site.emailUser }}" data-d="{{ site.emailDomain }}" href="#contact">{{ icons.mail | safe }}<span>{{ site.emailUser }} at {{ site.emailDomain | replace(".", " dot ") }}</span></a>
    {% for l in site.links %}<a class="pill" href="{{ l.url }}">{{ icons[l.icon] | safe }}{{ l.label }}</a>{% endfor %}
  </p>
</section>
